   "provider": "Dr. Jesus Robinson",
   "specialty": "family medicine",
   "page_count": 2,
   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "FAX 23  -- ROI --\nBates LLC Medical Group\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI was pleased to see John Stevens, a 70-year-old male patient of yours, in consultation on December 11, 2025. He presented for follow-up of his frailty findings and gout.\n\n**History:**\nMr. Stevens has a significant history of frailty findings, which have been controlled since their onset in 2011. He currently exhibits activities of daily living (ADL) dependency. Regarding his which began in 2022, he has been doing well with his current medication regimen of colchicine 0.6 mg daily. Unfortunately, I have noted that Mr. Stevens has been non-compliant with his prescribed medications and has missed his follow-up appointments on two occasions.\n\n**Examination:**\nDuring the visit, Mr. Stevens' vital signs were within normal limits, with a blood pressure of 137/70 mmHg and a weight of 184 pounds. His physical exam was otherwise unremarkable with normal cardiovascular, respiratory, and neurological findings. His joint examination revealed no active gout flares.\n\n**Impression:**\nMr. Stevens continues to manage his frailty findings effectively. His gout remains controlled with his current medication regimen, and there are no signs of active gout at this time. However, his non-compliance with medications and missed follow-up appointments are concerning and need to be addressed to prevent potential complications.\n\n**Recommendations:**\n1. **Medication Compliance:** I strongly encourage Mr. Stevens to adhere to his prescribed medication regimen for gout. This is critical for maintaining control of his condition and preventing future flares.\n2. **Follow-up Appointments:** It is essential that Mr. Stevens attends all scheduled follow-up appointments to monitor his conditions effectively. Regular check-ups will help in early detection and management of any potential issues.\n3. **Lifestyle Modifications:** Mr. Stevens should continue with his exercise routine, which includes running 3-4 times a week. This is beneficial for maintaining his overall health and managing his frailty.\n4. **Social Mr. Stevens uses chewing tobacco several times a day, a habit he started in 2016. He also consumes approximately eight alcoholic drinks per week. While these habits are not directly related to his current conditions, they are important factors to consider in his overall health and should be monitored.\n\nPlease continue to support Mr. Stevens in his efforts to adhere to his treatment plan and maintain regular follow-up appointments. I appreciate your collaboration in ensuring the best possible care for him.\n\nThank you for this ref"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "erral. Please feel free to reach out if you have any further questions or require additional information.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Jesus Robinson\nFamily Medicine\nBates LLC Medical Group\n"
    }
